UPDATE companies SET description='Foodberry is headquartered in Boston, Massachusetts. The company originated from research at Harvard and MIT, where founder David Edwards — a Harvard professor and serial entrepreneur — developed a plant-based coating technology to tackle two food-system problems: making convenient snacks nutritious and cutting plastic waste. The leadership team includes CEO Marty Kolewe (PhD, MIT/Johns Hopkins), board chair Stefan Catsicas (former Nestlé CTO), and operations head Jose Albelo. (No founding year disclosed.)

Foodberry runs a 42,000 sq ft, SQF Level 2–certified facility in Boston offering co-manufacturing, product development, and technology transfer. Its platform transforms foods and beverages — fruit, ice cream, yogurt, smoothies — into bite-sized, edible-coated snacks. The R&D team works with partners from concept to scale-up and can integrate the coating process into existing lines.

The company serves food and beverage brands in categories such as fruit snacks, frozen desserts, dairy, and convenience foods. Named partners include Bel Group (cheese and fruit-snack lines), Van Leeuwen (ice cream bonbons), Gopuff (ice cream bubbles), and Cape Cod Select (frozen smoothie bites).

Foodberry’s mission is to “make the future of snacking as nutritious, delicious and good for the planet as a natural berry.” Its differentiators are a proprietary, no-mess coating that reduces packaging, an end-to-end innovation model covering R&D through full-scale production, and GFSI-recognized food safety certification.', certifications=ARRAY['SQF Level 2','GFSI']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Product Development", "Co-Manufacturing", "Technology Transfer"], "industries": ["Food & Beverage", "Snack Foods", "Frozen Desserts", "Dairy & Cheese", "Fruit & Vegetable Processing", "Convenience Foods"], "materials": ["Plant-based coatings", "Fruit", "Ice cream", "Yogurt", "Smoothie", "Cheese"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Proprietary plant-based coating that turns any food or beverage into a bite-sized, self-contained snack", "42,000 sq ft SQF Level 2 certified co-manufacturing facility in Boston", "Harvard/MIT-originated R&D team with deep food-science expertise", "Technology transfer for seamless integration into partner production lines", "Established partnerships with major brands including Bel Group, Van Leeuwen, and Gopuff"], "facts_used": ["Boston, Massachusetts headquarters -> db", "Developed in labs at Harvard and MIT -> /about-us", "Founder David Edwards, professor at Harvard -> /about-us", "CEO Marty Kolewe, PhD Scientist, MIT, Johns Hopkins -> /about-us", "Board Chair Stefan Catsicas, former Nestle CTO -> /about-us", "Head of Operations Jose Albelo -> /about-us", "Proprietary plant-based coating technology -> /", "42,000 sq ft production facility in Boston, MA -> /", "GFSI / SQF Level 2 certified -> /", "Services: Product Development, Co-Manufacturing, Tech Transfer -> /", "Partnerships with Bel Group, Van Leeuwen, Gopuff, Cape Cod Select -> /", "Mission: make future of snacking nutritious, delicious, good for planet -> /about-us", "SQF certification -> db", "Company type: Contract manufacturer / job shop -> /", "Makes products: yes -> /"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "As a B2B innovation provider we offer the following services: Product Development, Co-Manufacturing, 42,000 sq ft production facility in Boston, MA, GFSI / SQF Level 2, Tech Transfer", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='foodberry' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Foodservice Equipment Agents (F.E.A.) was founded in 1996 in Placentia, California, as a manufacturer''s representative firm serving the foodservice equipment market across California and Nevada. The company was established to connect commercial kitchen operators with high-quality equipment brands.

F.E.A. represents a portfolio of equipment lines including Prática high-speed ovens, Hestan grills, Dry Ager aging cabinets, Mibrasa charcoal ovens, and others. In 2016 the firm launched a sister company, F.E.A. Service, which provides delivery, installation, warehousing, and distribution for several manufacturers. Its technicians are factory trained and authorized, using OEM parts to service brands such as Continental Refrigerator, Crown Verity, Electro Freeze, Federal Industries, Henkelman, Irinox, Moffat, Pizza Master, and Robot Coupe. The company also operates demonstration kitchens in Southern California, Northern California, and Las Vegas for hands-on equipment evaluation.

By representing manufacturers such as Prática, Hestan, Dry Ager, and Mibrasa, F.E.A. supplies equipment for cooking, refrigeration, food preparation, and specialty applications.

