UPDATE companies SET description='Forj Medical is headquartered in Arden Hills, Minnesota, with additional facilities in St. Paul and Vadnais Heights. The company operates as a contract design and manufacturing organization (CDMO) focused exclusively on medical devices. Founding year and ownership details are not publicly disclosed.

Forj Medical provides end-to-end contract design and manufacturing services for medical devices. Its capabilities span precision molding, printed circuit board assembly, automation, cable assembly, cleanroom operations, polymer and metal 3D printing, and supply chain management. The company also offers design and development services including full system development, electromagnetic sensor design, subassembly design, design for manufacturing and automation, prototyping, and process validation. With 450,000 square feet of manufacturing space across six global facilities, Forj assembles over 250 million devices and components annually and has accumulated more than four million hours of medical device engineering experience.

Forj Medical serves medical device original equipment manufacturers ranging from startups to Fortune 500 companies. Its customer base includes companies developing fluid and gas management systems, surgical energy devices, optical systems, electromagnetic navigation sensors, stimulation and active wearables, and consumable components. Notable collaborations include work with Conavi Medical on a surgical imaging device and with Vocxi Health to miniaturize a breath-based cancer detection platform.

Forj Medical positions itself as a fully integrated, medical-only CDMO that combines design, manufacturing, and operational support under one roof. The company emphasizes its vertically integrated in-house capabilities, global footprint with U.S. centers of excellence and near-shore/offshore options, and a quality system certified to ISO 13485 with five FDA establishment registrations.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001','ISO 13485','RoHS','FDA Establishment Registration']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Precision Molding", "PCBA Manufacturing", "Automation", "Cable Assembly", "Cleanroom Operations", "Polymer 3D Printing", "Metal 3D Printing", "Supply Chain Management", "Service & Maintenance", "Sustaining Engineering", "Packaging & Shipping", "Full Medical Device System Development", "Custom Electromechanical System Design", "Electromagnetic Sensor & Assembly Design", "Subassembly & Component Design", "Design for Excellence (DFX)", "Design for Manufacturing", "Design for Automation & Scale", "Custom Prototyping", "Process & Test Development", "Quality Management System (QMS)", "ISO 13485 Certification", "FDA Registration", "Vital Link Portal (Project Management & Compliance)"], "industries": ["Medical Device Manufacturing", "Fluid & Gas Management", "Surgical Energy", "Optical Systems", "Electromagnetic Navigation Systems & Sensors", "Stimulation & Active Wearables", "Consumables & Components"], "materials": ["Polymers", "Metals"], "equipment": [], "volume": "10 units to 10 million units", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["100% medical-focused contract design and manufacturing organization", "Vertically integrated in-house capabilities spanning design, molding, PCBA, automation, and cleanroom assembly", "Global footprint of six facilities totaling 450,000 square feet with U.S., near-shore, and offshore options", "ISO 13485 certified with five FDA establishment registrations", "Scalable production from prototype quantities to 10 million units annually"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Arden Hills, MN -> /", "Additional facilities in St. Paul and Vadnais Heights, MN -> /", "250+ million devices/components assembled per year -> /", "4+ million combined hours of medical device engineering -> /", "450,000 sq ft manufacturing space across 6 global facilities -> /", "Capabilities: Precision Molding, PCBA Manufacturing, Automation, Cable Assembly, Cleanrooms, Polymer & Metal 3D Printing -> /", "Design services: Full Medical Device System Development, Custom Electromechanical System Design, Electromagnetic Sensors & Assemblies, DFX, Prototyping -> /", "Industries: Fluid & Gas Management, Surgical Energy, Optical Systems, Electromagnetic Navigation Systems & Sensors, Stimulation & Active Wearables, Consumables & Components -> /", "Customer examples: Conavi Medical (Tom Looby), Vocxi Health, Fortune 500 Medical Device Manufacturer -> /", "Certifications: ISO 13485, five FDA Establishment Registrations, ISO 9001, CE Mark, RoHS -> /", "Scalable production from 10 units to 10 million -> /", "Vertically integrated in-house capabilities -> /", "Vital Link Portal for 24/7 project management and compliance access -> /", "Company type: CDMO (Contract Design and Manufacturing Organization) -> /", "Materials: Polymers & Metals -> /", "Minimum order: 10 units -> /"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Forj Medical, a global medical device Contract Design and Manufacturing Organization (CDMO)", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "10 units", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='forj-medical' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='FormTight, Inc. was founded in 1992 and is headquartered in Denver, Colorado. The company operates as a custom plastic thermoforming specialist, though the input does not specify its ownership structure or founders by name.

The company provides thin- and thick-gauge thermoforming for food, medical, industrial, and retail packaging. All stages—consultation, design, prototyping, mold manufacturing, 5-axis CNC routing, and production—are performed in-house at its Denver facility. It works with materials including PET, PVC, ABS, HIPS, HDPE, PP, PETG, and polycarbonate. No facility size, headcount, or annual volume figures are disclosed.

FormTight serves customers ranging from small manufacturers to larger firms across the food, medical, industrial, and retail sectors. Named references include Innovative Brick Systems (Denver), Dazzling Displays, Taylor Tools (Denver), Camerons Products (Colorado Springs), Arm Automation (Austin, TX), and an inventor in Portland, CT.

FormTight emphasizes attention to detail, competitive pricing, on-time delivery, and high-quality finished parts. It operates an in-house grinding system that recycles scrap back to suppliers, and highlights its ability to select alternative tooling approaches (such as male versus female molds) to solve difficult part geometries.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Thin gauge thermoforming", "Thick gauge thermoforming", "Custom packaging design", "Plastic prototyping", "Mold manufacturing", "5-axis CNC routing", "In-house scrap grinding and recycling", "Material selection and processing (PET, PVC, ABS, HIPS, HDPE, PP, PETG, PC)", "Tooling fabrication", "Consultation and design support", "Production thermoforming"], "industries": ["Food packaging", "Medical packaging", "Industrial thermoforming", "Retail packaging"], "materials": ["PET (Polyethylene Terephthalate)", "PVC (Polyvinyl Chloride)", "ABS (Acrylonitrile Butadiene Styrene)", "HIPS (High Impact Polystyrene)", "HDPE (High Density Polyethylene)", "PP (Polypropylene)", "PETG (Polyethylene Terephthalate Glycol)", "PC (Polycarbonates)"], "equipment": ["5-axis CNC router", "In-house grinding system", "Tooling foundry (partner)"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["All process stages (design through production) under one roof in Denver", "In-house scrap grinding and closed-loop recycling with material suppliers", "5-axis CNC routing for trim and secondary operations", "Rapid prototyping turnaround for custom packaging", "Tooling expertise including male/female mold selection"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1992, headquartered in Denver, CO -> /about-us", "Specializes in thin and thick gauge thermoforming for food, medical, industrial, retail -> /about-us", "All stages in-house: consultation, design, prototyping, mold manufacturing, production, 5-axis CNC routing -> /about-us", "Materials: PET, PVC, ABS, HIPS, HDPE, PP, PETG, PC -> / (contact form) and /services", "In-house grinding operation for scrap recycling -> /about-us", "Customer examples: Innovative Brick Systems, Dazzling Displays, Taylor Tools, Camerons Products, Arm Automation, Steven R. Knight -> /about-us testimonials", "Over 30 years experience -> /about-us", "Capabilities: custom packaging design, thin gauge, thick gauge, prototyping, mold manufacturing, 5-axis routing -> /services", "Focus on attention to detail, competitive pricing, on-time delivery, high-quality -> /about-us", "Tooling fabrication capability, male vs female tool selection -> /about-us testimonial (Stephen Grupinski)"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Founded in 1992, FormTight is a custom plastic thermoforming company headquartered in Denver, CO.", "founded_year": "1992", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='formtight-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Formel Industries Packaging operates from Franklin Park, Illinois, producing flexible packaging for a range of consumer and industrial markets. The company''s founding year and ownership structure are not publicly disclosed.

The company manufactures printed roll stock, pre-formed pouches, laminated films, heat-transfer labels, Inno-Lok® pre-zippered films, lidding films, cellophane and polypropylene bags, stand-up pouches, and vertical form-fill-seal and flow-wrap packaging. It also supplies high-moisture-barrier films and oriented polypropylene (OPP and BOPP) films. Production capabilities include a 10-color W&H Miraflex press installed in 2023 and a regenerative thermal oxidizer for emissions control.

Customers span medical device manufacturing, confectionery, pail production, private-label oils, and food packaging. A senior buyer at a large medical corporation noted the firm''s ISO 13485 and FDA compliance, while a VP of procurement at a American confectioner and a purchasing manager at a private-label oil producer cited reliability and responsiveness.

Formel emphasizes environmental responsibility, highlighting its regenerative thermal oxidizer and a stated sustainability vision. Customers consistently reference on-time delivery, quality ratings, and the ability to accommodate rush orders and last-minute changes.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 13485']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Flexible packaging manufacturing", "Printed roll stock production", "Pre-formed pouch making", "Film lamination", "Heat transfer labeling", "Inno-Lok\u00ae pre-zippered film application", "Lidding film production", "Cellophane and polypropylene bag making", "Stand-up pouch manufacturing", "Vertical form-fill-seal packaging", "Flow wrap packaging", "High moisture barrier film production", "Oriented polypropylene (OPP/BOPP) film production", "Regenerative thermal oxidation (emissions control)", "10-color rotogravure/flexographic printing"], "industries": ["Medical devices", "Confectionery", "Pail manufacturing", "Private label oils", "Food packaging"], "materials": ["Polypropylene", "Cellophane", "Oriented Polypropylene (OPP)", "Oriented Polypropylene (BOPP)", "High moisture barrier films", "Laminated films"], "equipment": ["Regenerative Thermal Oxidizer", "10-Color W&H Miraflex Press"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["10-color W&H Miraflex press for high-definition printing", "Regenerative thermal oxidizer for emissions control", "ISO 13485 certification for medical device packaging", "Stated commitment to environmental sustainability"], "facts_used": ["Location: Franklin Park, Illinois -> db", "Certification: ISO 13485 -> db", "Products: printed roll stock, pre-formed pouches, laminated films, heat transfer labels, Inno-Lok pre-zippered films, lidding films, cellophane & polypropylene bags, stand-up pouches, VFFS packaging, flow wrap packaging, high moisture barrier film, OPP/BOPP films -> /", "Equipment: Regenerative Thermal Oxidizer -> / (news July 2023)", "Equipment: 10-Color W&H Miraflex Press -> /