UPDATE companies SET description='Based in Conway, Arkansas, Fortier, Inc. operates as a commercial design and equipment supply firm specializing in space optimization and traffic flow layout design.

Fortier provides turnkey services that span commercial interior design, store layout planning, CAD design, equipment sales consulting, warehousing, and installation.

Its customer base includes convenience stores, liquor stores, and grocery departments, where the company designs layouts for product placement, customer flow, and operational efficiency. Fortier also serves broader commercial interior projects requiring integrated equipment supply and installation, emphasizing a local presence with sales offices ready to assist.

The company emphasizes professionalism, excellence, and timeliness as core differentiators, promoting a reputation for responsive and generous service. A turnkey approach and local sales offices are highlighted as key advantages for clients seeking a single point of contact for design, equipment, and installation.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Turnkey services", "Commercial design consulting", "Store layout design", "Convenience store design planning", "CAD design", "Equipment sales consulting", "Warehousing installation", "Commercial interiors design", "Equipment supply"], "industries": ["Convenience stores", "Liquor stores", "Grocery departments", "Commercial interiors"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Turnkey services covering design, equipment, and installation", "Local sales offices for hands-on support", "Commitment to professionalism, excellence, and timeliness", "Responsive and generous service reputation", "CAD design and equipment consulting capabilities"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters: Conway, Arkansas -> db", "Services: Turnkey services, commercial design consulting, store layout design, CAD design, equipment sales consulting, warehousing installation -> page /", "Industries served: Convenience stores, liquor stores, grocery departments, commercial interiors -> page /", "Differentiators: Professionalism, Excellence, Timeliness; Local and ready to help; Turnkey services -> page /", "Company type: Commercial Design & Equipment Supply Company -> page /"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Commercial Design & Equipment Supply Company", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='fortier-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Forum Plastics LLC operates from Watertown, Connecticut, where it was founded in 1992 as GM Tool & Forum Molding Inc. The business was consolidated under the Forum Plastics name in 2009 and became part of the Squadron Capital group of companies in 2016, which reinvests proceeds into technology upgrades.

As a full-service contract manufacturer, Forum provides injection molding, micro molding, insert and over molding, cleanroom assembly in an ISO Class 7 environment, mold design and fabrication, machining, pad printing, laser marking, and rapid prototyping. The company runs a 101-person operation in a facility that added 10,000 square feet in 2015 and relocated to a new building in December 2025, producing 100,000 to 200,000 parts per month.

Forum serves medical device and life science OEMs and startups, as well as industrial and military/defense customers. Its client base ranges from early-stage ventures needing prototype volumes to global original equipment manufacturers requiring full-scale commercialization support.

The company emphasizes an engineering-based, customer-first approach, offering design-for-manufacturability guidance, project management, and quality systems certified to ISO 13485:2016 and ISO 14001:2015, with ITAR registration. Squadron Capital backing enables continuous investment in advanced equipment such as CT scanning, micro molding presses, and additive manufacturing.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 13485:2016','ISO 9001:2008','ISO 14001:2015','ITAR registration']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Cleanroom assembly (ISO Class 7)", "Injection molding", "Insert molding", "Over molding", "Micro molding", "Mold design & fabrication", "CNC machining", "EDM machining", "Precision grinding & polishing", "Pad printing", "Laser marking", "Quick-turn prototyping", "Quality & metrology (CMM, VMM, CT scanning, FAI, IQ/OQ/PQ, PPAP, Gage R&R)", "Engineering & program management", "Design for manufacturability (DFM)", "Kitting & sterile packaging (through partners)", "Serialization services", "Mold financing", "MoldFlow simulation", "Additive manufacturing (3D printing)", "Automated inspection", "CT scanning services"], "industries": ["Medical devices", "Life sciences", "Industrial", "Military/Defense"], "materials": ["Medical-grade plastics", "Engineering-grade plastics"], "equipment": ["BOY Mini Molders", "Arburg Shuttle Press", "Arburg Micro Molders", "Arburg 220 & 270 Ton Molding Cells", "Keyence IM", "Keyence IL", "CT Scanner", "3D Systems Printer", "Filament 3D Printer", "Additive Freeform 3D Printer", "CNC machining centers", "EDM machines", "Precision grinding and polishing centers", "Coordinate Measuring Machine (CMM)", "Vision Measuring Machine (VMM)"], "volume": "100,000-200,000 parts per month; prototype to production volumes", "lead_time": "Days for prototypes; quick-turn prototyping", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["ISO Class 7 cleanroom molding and assembly", "Micro molding capability for parts as small as 0.005 in\u00b3", "In-house mold design, fabrication, and repair with full-service tool room", "ITAR registered for defense work", "Rapid prototyping delivering parts in days, not months"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1992 as GM Tool & Forum Molding Inc. -> /about-us", "Headquartered in Watertown, Connecticut -> /about-us", "Consolidated under Forum Plastics Inc. in 2009 -> /about-us", "Sold to Squadron Capital in 2016 -> /about-us", "ISO 13485:2016 certified -> /quality", "ISO 9001:2008 certified -> /about-us", "ISO 14001:2015 certified -> /about-us", "ITAR registration achieved 2020 -> /about-us", "ISO Class 7 cleanroom molding and assembly -> /capabilities", "Produces 100,000-200,000 parts per month -> /", "101 employees overseen by Director of Operations -> /about-us", "Serves medical, industrial, military/defense industries -> /", "Micro molding capability down to 0.005 in\u00b3 -> /capabilities", "In-house mold design, fabrication, and repair -> /capabilities", "Rapid prototyping to production in days -> /", "Engineering-based company with DFM support -> /capabilities", "Equipment: BOY Mini Molders, Arburg presses, CT scanner, Keyence systems, 3D printers -> /about-us", "Facility: 10,000 sq ft addition 2015, moved to new facility Dec 2025 -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Forum is a full-service contract manufacturer that has served the medical device and life science industries for over 34 years.", "founded_year": "1992", "employee_count": "101", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": ["ITAR registered"], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='forum-plastics-llc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Four Engines Apparel operates from a shop at 201B West Boylston Street in West Boylston, Massachusetts. The company was established in 2020 by Dave Keddy, who began the venture as a home-based operation focused on quality decorations and personal customer service. After building a customer base, Keddy moved the business out of his basement into its current dedicated facility.

The shop provides apparel decoration services including embroidery, screen printing, custom patches, and heat transfers. Keddy brings over 17 years of experience in logo merchandising, having started in screen printing in 2012 after working in paper and plastic printing. The operation handles orders across various garment types and materials, producing branded gear for clients ranging from single pieces to larger runs.

Customers include local small businesses, musical acts, sports teams, and event organizers. The company has produced custom hats for a Las Vegas show, embroidered jackets for a soccer season, and show shirts for Expedition Reptile, a performing group that washes garments weekly. Keddy emphasizes serving small companies that larger facilities often turn away due to low minimum quantities.

The business was founded partly to fill a gap for low-quantity orders that larger print shops decline. A longer-term mission aims to partner with a local charity to fund community music programs, reflecting Keddy''s background as a musician and the company''s name, inspired by a drumming term. The owner cites a personal drive for consistency and attention to detail as core to the work.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Embroidery", "Screen Printing", "Custom Patches", "Heat Transfers", "Logo Merchandising", "Custom Apparel Decoration"], "industries": ["Music and Entertainment", "Small Business", "Sports Teams", "Event Merchandise", "Reptile Shows", "Community Organizations"], "materials": ["Various apparel fabrics"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Accepts low-quantity orders that larger facilities decline", "Owner-operated with over 17 years in logo merchandising", "Personal customer service and direct communication", "Fast turnaround on tight deadlines", "Showcases actual completed work rather than stock imagery"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2020, home-based then shop in West Boylston, MA -> /", "Owner Dave Keddy -> / (reviews)", "Services: embroidery, screen printing, patches, transfers -> /", "Over 17 years experience in logo merchandising, started screen printing 2012 -> /about", "Accepts low-quantity orders larger facilities decline -> /about", "Mission to help small companies and music programs -> /about", "Custom hats for Las Vegas show -> / (review)", "Jackets for soccer season -> / (review)", "Show shirts for Expedition Reptile -> / (review)", "Address: 201B W Boylston St, West Boylston, MA 01583 -> /", "Phone and email -> /"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Four Engines Apparel began as a home-based company dedicated to quality decorations and personal customer service", "founded_year": "2020", "employee_count": "", "cag