UPDATE companies SET description='Full Spectrum Solar was founded in August 2002 in Madison, Wisconsin, by brothers Burke and Mark O''Neal, both University of Wisconsin–Madison mechanical engineering alumni. After Burke returned from a lead engineering role at a large California solar firm, the pair set out to build a Wisconsin-based solar contractor grounded in engineering rigor, quality installation, and long-term customer support. The company remains family-owned and operated.

The firm designs and installs solar photovoltaic systems, home battery backup, electric-vehicle charging stations, and heat-pump water heaters, and provides ongoing maintenance, repair, and storm-damage restoration for existing arrays. Its in-house team includes mechanical and electrical engineers, master and journeyman electricians, NABCEP-certified professionals, experienced roofers, and dedicated project managers. Since inception, Full Spectrum Solar has completed more than 1,500 installations totaling over 28 megawatts of capacity across southern Wisconsin, operating from offices in Madison and Waukesha.

Customers range from homeowners and farms to multifamily housing, healthcare facilities, recreation centers, offices, schools, public agencies, and nonprofit organizations. The portfolio includes ground-mounted arrays for agricultural operations, rooftop systems for commercial buildings, and community-scale projects for municipalities and nonprofits throughout the region.

The company distinguishes itself through an education-first approach—no commissioned salespeople—direct pricing, a single accountable project manager for each job, and a post-installation service department that remains available long after commissioning. Its Madison headquarters earned an ENERGY STAR 100/100 rating, and the firm emphasizes transparent communication, practical system recommendations, and standing behind its work for the life of the system.', certifications=ARRAY['NABCEP']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Solar photovoltaic system design and installation", "Home battery backup system installation", "Electric vehicle charging station installation", "Heat pump water heater installation", "Solar system maintenance and repair", "Storm damage assessment and solar removal/reinstallation", "Roofing coordination for solar projects", "Project management and permitting", "System monitoring and performance support", "Engineering and feasibility analysis"], "industries": ["Residential", "Commercial", "Agricultural", "Nonprofit", "Public sector", "Multifamily housing", "Healthcare", "Recreation", "Education"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["No commissioned salespeople", "Dedicated project manager for each project", "In-house post-installation service department", "Direct pricing with practical system recommendations", "NABCEP-certified professionals on staff"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2002 by Burke and Mark O''Neal -> /about-us", "Family-owned -> /about-us", "1,500+ systems installed, 28+ MW capacity -> /about-us", "Services: solar electric, battery backup, EV charging, heat pump water heaters, maintenance, storm damage -> /services", "Serves residential, commercial, agricultural, nonprofit, public sector -> /about-us", "NABCEP-certified professionals on staff -> /about-us", "ENERGY STAR 100/100 rating for headquarters -> /about-us", "No commissioned salespeople, dedicated project manager, in-house service department -> /", "Direct pricing, certified master electricians -> /", "24 years experience, 1,600+ installation locations -> /", "Best of Madison awards 2023-2026 -> /"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Full Spectrum Solar is a family-owned Wisconsin company built around engineering, craftsmanship, clear guidance, and support that continues long after installation.", "founded_year": "2002", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned", "Small business"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='full-spectrum-solar' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Furniture Classics operates from a 10,000-square-foot showroom at 433 West 5th Avenue in Anchorage, Alaska. The business traces its roots to the late 1950s when Anchorage pioneer Helen Calrquist opened Eckman''s on 4th Avenue. After a bank takeover, she relocated to 5th Avenue. The store later became Nerland''s Home Furnishings under the Nerland family, with longtime sales associate Erma Howell. In 1989, Howell partnered with current owner Colleen Hickey to establish Furniture Classics.

As a furniture retailer and interior design studio, Furniture Classics offers a rotating inventory of American-made furniture, custom orders with over 2,000 fabric options, interior design services (many complimentary), white-glove delivery and installation across Anchorage and surrounding areas, and furniture assembly. The showroom spans 10,000 square feet and carries pieces in solid walnut, maple, cherry, leather, and velvet. Financing is available with 18 months deferred interest on purchases over $1,500.

The company serves residential customers throughout Alaska, including homeowners in Anchorage, Girdwood, Eagle River, and the Matanuska-Susitna Valley. They also cater to customers looking for custom-made furniture and one-of-a-kind pieces sourced from national markets such as High Point.

Furniture Classics'' stated mission is to provide quality American-made furniture to Alaskans at an affordable price without sacrificing comfort or style. The team emphasizes its 35-plus years of industry experience, which allows it to curate durable, high-quality brands and avoid lower-quality imitations. Designers help clients navigate thousands of fabric and style options to create functional, beautiful spaces.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom furniture orders", "Interior design consultation", "White-glove delivery and installation", "Furniture assembly", "In-store showroom shopping", "Financing (18 months deferred interest)", "Custom fabric selection (2,000+ fabrics)", "One-of-a-kind piece sourcing from national markets"], "industries": ["Residential furniture", "Interior design", "Home furnishings"], "materials": ["Walnut", "Maple", "Cherry", "Leather", "Fabric", "Velvet"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Over 2,000 fabric options for custom orders", "Complimentary interior design services", "White-glove delivery and installation across Anchorage and surrounding areas", "Same-day take-home from showroom floor", "35+ years of experience curating American-made brands"], "facts_used": ["Location: 433 West 5th Avenue, Anchorage, Alaska -> /", "Showroom size: 10,000 square feet -> /", "Founding story: Helen Calrquist (1950s), Nerland family, Erma Howell, Colleen Hickey (1989) -> /about", "Woman-owned: ''proud of our connection to intrepid female Alaskan entrepreneurs'' -> /about", "Custom fabric options: over 2,000 fabrics -> /", "Complimentary interior design services -> /", "White-glove delivery to Anchorage, Girdwood, Eagle River, Valley -> /", "Same-day take-home from showroom -> /", "35+ years experience curating American-made brands -> /", "Financing: 18 months deferred interest on $1,500+ -> /", "Materials: walnut, maple, cherry, leather, velvet, fabric -> /", "Database founde