UPDATE companies SET description='GAI Energy, based in Flora, Indiana, was founded in 2008 by electrical engineers Chris Rohaly and Neal Rhodes in nearby Kokomo. The company, now led by CEO Cindy Rohaly, CTO Chris Rohaly, and COO Lamar Sledge, began with a mission to deliver high-quality renewable energy systems to the Hoosier state.

The firm operates as an EPC (engineering, procurement, and construction) contractor specializing in turnkey solar photovoltaic and battery storage installations, as well as microgrid systems. Its in-house team handles design, permitting, procurement, construction, and ongoing operations and maintenance. To date, the company has installed more than 14.5 megawatts of capacity across projects ranging from kilowatt-scale to megawatt-scale systems.

GAI Energy serves commercial, industrial, and agricultural customers throughout north-central Indiana, including farmers, business owners, and utility partners. The company references installations in communities such as Lafayette, Plymouth, Valparaiso, and Carmel, and works closely with local permitting jurisdictions and utility companies.

The founders aimed to exceed the state''s minimum electrical code requirements; every project is built to the 2020 National Electrical Code and UL safety standards, with a preference for North American-made components. By managing the full project lifecycle without subcontracting, GAI Energy says it eliminates markups and delivers optimized, client-specific designs rather than cookie-cutter solutions.', certifications=ARRAY['UL safety standards','National Electrical Code 2020']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Solar PV system design", "Solar PV installation", "Battery energy storage system installation", "Microgrid design and installation", "Electrical engineering", "Permitting and utility interconnection", "Operations and maintenance", "EPC (Engineering, Procurement, Construction) services"], "industries": ["Commercial", "Industrial", "Agricultural", "Utility"], "materials": ["Solar PV modules", "Battery storage systems", "Electrical balance-of-system components"], "equipment": [], "volume": "Kilowatt to megawatt scale systems", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["UL-listed components and North American-made products where possible", "In-house EPC model eliminates subcontractor markups", "Designs optimized per client, not cookie-cutter", "Ongoing operations and maintenance offered post-installation"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2008 -> db, /about", "Founders Chris Rohaly and Neal Rhodes -> /about", "Headquarters Flora, Indiana -> db, /about", "18+ years in business -> /", "52 years combined solar experience -> /", "14.5 MW installed capacity -> /", "Services: EPC solar, battery storage, microgrid -> /, /about", "Industries: commercial, industrial, agricultural -> /about", "Leadership team: Chris Rohaly (CTO), Cindy Rohaly (CEO), Lamar Sledge (COO) -> /about", "Quality standards: NEC 2020, UL -> /about", "In-house EPC, no subcontracting -> /about", "Ongoing O&M -> /about", "North American made products -> /about", "Service area: north-central Indiana -