UPDATE companies SET description='GT Sales is headquartered in Salt Lake City, Utah, with its physical location on Parkway Boulevard in West Valley City. The company was founded in 1965 by Gordon Tyler as a manufacturer''s representative for both electrical supply and lighting lines. The lighting side of the agency was spun off in the mid-1980s, leaving the firm focused solely on electrical products. In May 1997, Tyler sold the business to Daryl Cook, who had been in electrical distribution since 1975. Cook moved the operation to its current site in early 1999 and purchased the building in 2003, quadrupling the available space from 5,000 to 20,000 square feet.

The firm acts as a manufacturer''s representative and stocking distributor for more than a dozen electrical brands, including Arlington Industries, Elite Components, MGM Transformer, RectorSeal, and Voltec. The 20,000-square-foot warehouse is complemented by a fenced 15,000-square-foot yard and a 2,500-square-foot office with a conference room. A team of 11 handles inside and outside sales, logistics, and warehouse operations across the region.

GT Sales serves electrical wholesalers and distributors in the commercial, residential, education, HVAC, utility, and industrial sectors. Its territory covers the Intermountain West: Utah, southern Idaho, eastern Nevada, western Wyoming, and Montana. The company positions itself as the liaison between manufacturers and distributors, helping wholesalers access new products and stay current on technology.

The company''s stated mission is to empower progress by connecting customers with the highest-quality electrical solutions, built on lasting partnerships, trust, and innovation. Core values emphasized by leadership include integrity, innovation, partnership, excellence, and commitment.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Manufacturer representation", "Sales and marketing support", "Product training", "Technical support", "Warehousing and distribution", "Inventory management", "Liaison between manufacturers and distributors"], "industries": ["Commercial", "Residential", "Education", "HVAC", "Utility", "Industrial", "Electrical wholesale"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["20,000 sq ft warehouse with 15,000 sq ft fenced yard", "Stocking distributor for 14+ leading electrical manufacturers", "Product training and technical support for wholesale partners", "Five-state coverage across the Intermountain West"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1965 by Gordon Tyler -> /about", "Sold to Daryl Cook in 1997 -> /about", "Moved to Parkway Boulevard in 1999, building purchased 2003 -> /about", "20,000 sq ft warehouse, 15,000 sq ft yard, 2,500 sq ft office -> /", "11 team members -> /", "Represents 14+ manufacturers including Arlington Industries, Elite Components, MGM Transformer -> /", "Serves commercial, residential, education, HVAC, utility, industrial markets -> /", "Territory: Utah, southern Idaho, eastern Nevada, western Wyoming, Montana -> /", "Mission, vision, core values stated -> /about"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Manufacturer''s representatives play a crucial role in the electrical wholesale industry across the Intermountain West. We act as a liaison between manufacturers and distributors.", "founded_year": "1965", "employee_count": "11", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='gt-sales-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Galaxy Wire & Cable, Inc. is based in Horsham, Pennsylvania. Founded in 1995 by industry veteran Kathy Stussy, the company began as a woman-owned business after Stussy identified a market need for custom wire and cable products with quick deliveries and low minimum quantities. The firm is certified as a women''s business enterprise (WBENC) and operates as a Disadvantaged Business Enterprise (DBE) in Pennsylvania, California, Texas, and Illinois.

The company designs and manufactures custom wire, cable, and cable assemblies from prototype through large production runs. Its capabilities span custom cable construction—including conductor selection, shielding, insulation, and jacketing materials—as well as wire harness and cable assembly manufacturing. Galaxy added an assembly division in 2003 and provides engineering design services alongside production and testing.

Galaxy serves defense customers as an ITAR-registered supplier and supports transportation projects through its DBE certifications for Department of Transportation-funded work. The company also supplies a variety of industrial sectors requiring custom wire and cable solutions.

Galaxy differentiates itself with a "one-stop shop" model that combines wire, cable, and assembly production under one roof, backed by ISO 9001 quality certification since 2014. The company emphasizes low minimum orders, rapid turnaround, and engineering support to meet exact specifications.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001','ITAR','WBENC','DBE (Pennsylvania)','DBE (California)','DBE (Texas)','DBE (Illinois)']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom wire and cable design and construction", "Cable and wire assembly manufacturing", "Wire harness manufacturing", "Prototype and low-volume production", "Large production runs", "Engineering design services", "Quality control and assurance", "ISO 9001 quality management"], "industries": ["Defense", "Transportation"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "Prototype to large production runs", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["One-stop shop for wire, cable, and assemblies", "Low minimum order requirements", "Engineering design services from prototype to production", "ITAR registered for defense work", "Woman-owned (WBENC) and DBE certified in four states"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1995 by Kathy Stussy -> /about", "Woman-owned, WBENC certified -> /about", "ISO 9001 certification achieved in 2014 -> /about", "ITAR registered with DDTC -> /about", "DBE certified in Pennsylvania, California, Texas, Illinois -> /about", "Assembly Division started in 2003 -> /about", "Headquarters in Horsham, Pennsylvania -> db", "Custom wire and cable design and construction -> /about", "Cable/wire assemblies and harnesses manufacturing -> /about", "Low minimum order requirements -> /about", "Engineering design services -> /about", "One-stop shop for wire, cable, and assemblies -> /about", "Over 50 years of collective experience -> /about", "Quality control and assurance -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Galaxy Wire & Cable, Inc. is a leading cable and wire manufacturer and supplier", "founded_year": "1995", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "Low minimum order requirements", "export_compliance": ["ITAR registered"], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/galaxy-wire-and-cable/"], "ownership_tags": ["Woman-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='galaxy-wire-and-cable' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Galesburg Electric/Industrial Supply, Inc. was founded in 1951 in Galesburg, Illinois, by Hilding and Lucile Johnson. The couple envisioned a business that went beyond simply supplying materials to local residents, contractors, and municipalities; they wanted to stand behind the merchandise and ensure every employee had deep product knowledge and a commitment to customer satisfaction. The company has remained family-run since its inception, with their son Craig joining eight years later and later serving as CEO and chairman, and their daughter Barbara helping launch the firm''s online division, tanforless.com.

It stocks brands such as Baldor, Leviton, ABB, Appleton, Bussmann, and Cooper B-Line. Sales are conducted through a physical location in Galesburg and an e-commerce platform that has been active since 1997. The firm also supplies repair parts for equipment from manufacturers like Milwaukee, DeWalt, and Generac.

Primary customers are electrical contractors, municipal agencies, industrial facilities, and residential buyers, with a noted focus on energy management applications.

