UPDATE companies SET description='General Spring of Kansas City, Inc. operates from New Century, Kansas, in the Kansas City metropolitan area. The company was founded in 1965 by Paul Flood, who envisioned a full-service repair shop specializing in automotive leaf springs. After Flood’s brother Jim took over in 1985 and moved operations to Olathe, the business passed to Jim’s son, Jim Jr., and later to Joe Wallace in 2004.

The company manufactures and supplies leaf springs, coil springs, shackles, U-bolts, shocks, and add-a-leaf kits for a wide range of vehicles. It maintains in-house manufacturing and modification capabilities, allowing customization of stock leaf springs to customer specifications, such as replacing stock clips with metal riveted clips for added strength. General Spring also warehouses products at its Kansas City location and ships from multiple distribution points nationwide, visually inspecting each part before dispatch.

General Spring serves both DIY enthusiasts and professional suspension repair shops across the automotive aftermarket. Its product line covers light trucks, heavy-duty trucks, SUVs, and off-road vehicles, with specific applications for brands including Chevrolet, Ford, Jeep, Toyota, and Nissan. The company also supports fleet and commercial customers needing heavy-duty suspension upgrades.

General Spring differentiates itself by working exclusively with manufacturers that are full members of the Spring Research Institute, ensuring high quality-control standards. It offers a one-year warranty on all replacement leaf springs, guarantees products meet or exceed OEM specifications, and provides fast shipping—most stocked items ship within 24 hours. The company emphasizes knowledgeable customer support and the ability to customize springs for unique requirements.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Leaf spring manufacturing", "Coil spring manufacturing", "Shackle manufacturing", "U-bolt manufacturing", "Shock and strut supply", "Add-a-leaf kit assembly", "Suspension part customization", "Quality inspection", "Warehousing and distribution", "Custom leaf spring modification"], "industries": ["Automotive aftermarket", "Light truck", "Heavy-duty truck", "SUV", "Off-road", "Suspension repair"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "24-hour shipping for stocked items", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Works exclusively with Spring Research Institute (SRI) member manufacturers", "Visually inspects every part before shipping", "One-year warranty on all replacement leaf springs", "Products meet or exceed OEM specifications", "In-house manufacturing and modification for custom spring configurations", "Most stocked items ship within 24 hours"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1965 by Paul Flood -> /about-us", "Family ownership succession (Jim Flood, Jim Jr., Joe Wallace) -> /about-us", "Headquarters in New Century, Kansas -> db", "18,000-square-foot facility added in 2014 -> /about-us", "In-house manufacturing and modification capabilities -> /", "Customization of stock leaf springs (e.g., riveted clips) -> /", "Warehousing at Kansas City location and shipping from multiple distribution points -> /about-us", "Visual inspection of all parts before shipping -> /", "One-year warranty on replacement leaf springs -> /", "Products meet or exceed OEM specifications -> /", "Work exclusively with Spring Research Institute (SRI) member manufacturers -> /", "Fast shipping: most items within 24 hours -> /", "Serves DIY enthusiasts and suspension repair professionals -> /", "Brands served: Chevrolet, Ford, Jeep, Toyota, Nissan -> /about-us", "Product range: leaf springs, coil springs, shackles, U-bolts, shocks, add-a-leaf kits -> /, /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We also have extensive in-house manufacturing and modification capabilities, so we can customize any stock leaf spring to your specifications.", "founded_year": "1965", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='general-spring-of-kansas-city-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='General Woodworking Inc was founded in 1978 in Lowell, Massachusetts, as a family-owned business. The company is owned by John Thompson, Sara Axon, and Dan Thompson, and has served general contractors and end users across New England for over four decades.

The firm operates a 46,300-square-foot, solar-powered manufacturing facility in historic Lowell, where it produces architectural millwork and decorative laid-up panels. Its capabilities span complete project execution—from design and engineering to AWI QCP-certified fabrication—and it holds FSC® Chain-of-Custody certification (FSC® C106456) for responsibly sourced lumber and veneer. The staff includes numerous employees with 20 to 30 years of tenure, preserving deep institutional knowledge.

