UPDATE companies SET description='Gentuity, LLC is based in Sudbury, Massachusetts. The company was founded by veterans of the original LightLab team that pioneered the first-generation optical coherence tomography (OCT) systems used in catheterization laboratories worldwide. Drawing on decades of experience advancing intravascular imaging, the founders set out to develop a next-generation OCT platform that would overcome the limitations of traditional systems.

The high-frequency OCT technology captures a full-length coronary image in a single one-second pullback, delivering a comprehensive view of the artery. The system is designed for plug-and-play integration into existing cath lab workflows without the need for sterile bags.

The technology targets interventional cardiologists performing percutaneous coronary intervention (PCI) for coronary artery disease. Clinical case studies highlight use at institutions such as Tampa General Hospital and The Christ Hospital. In 2026, Gentuity announced that its advanced intravascular imaging solutions would become available in the United States through a distribution partnership with GE HealthCare.

The company states its mission is to "cross new frontiers in cardiovascular care so patients can focus on living," emphasizing that clearer visualization leads to more informed treatment decisions. Gentuity differentiates itself with the Vis-Rx catheter''s ultra-low profile, rapid one-second imaging, and workflow simplicity, aiming to provide confidence at every step of complex PCI procedures.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["High-frequency OCT (HF-OCT) imaging system development", "Ultra-low-profile catheter design and manufacturing", "Intravascular imaging technology R&D", "Clinical case study research and publication", "Physician education and training resources"], "industries": ["Interventional cardiology", "Coronary artery disease treatment", "Percutaneous coronary intervention (PCI)", "Catheterization laboratory equipment", "Cardiovascular medical devices"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["1.8F ultra-low-profile catheter for small, tortuous vessels", "Full-length coronary imaging in a single one-second pullback", "Plug-and-play system integration without sterile bags", "High-frequency OCT (HF-OCT) technology", "U.S. distribution partnership with GE HealthCare"], "facts_used": ["Company name Gentuity, LLC -> db", "Headquarters Sudbury, Massachusetts -> db", "Founded by original LightLab team members -> /about-us", "Pioneered first-generation OCT systems -> /about-us", "Decades of experience advancing intravascular imaging -> /about-us", "Developed next-generation HF-OCT technology -> /about-us", "Product: HF-OCT Imaging System with Vis-Rx PRIME Micro-Imaging Catheter (1.8F) -> /", "Features: ultra-low-profile access, full-length imaging in one second, plug-and-play integration -> /", "Partnership with GE HealthCare for US distribution -> /", "Clinical case studies with Dr. Hiram Bezerra and Dr. Timothy Henry -> /", "Trademarks: HF-OCT, One Second Imaging, Vis-Rx -> /", "Mission: cross new frontiers in cardiovascular care -> /about-us", "Leadership team expertise in interventional cardiology, intravascular imaging, medical device innovation -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Gentuity is pioneering the next generation of intravascular imaging. Through high-frequency OCT (HF-OCT) and ultra-low-profile catheter technology, we''re giving interventional cardiologists complete vessel visualization and real-time insights to optimize PCI procedures for coronary artery disease.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='gentuity-llc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='George C. Moore, a family-owned manufacturer of narrow elastic fabrics and rigid webbing, traces its roots to 1909 when George C. Moore founded the company in Westerly, Rhode Island. The business remains privately held and operates as the parent of two wholly owned divisions: the original George C. Moore Company, focused on stretch and rigid narrow fabrics (woven and knit), and Darlington Fabrics, which produces stretch and rigid wide warp‑knit fabrics.

Today the company runs a U.S. headquarters in Westerly that houses sales, engineering, design, R&D, and technical support, while a 2006 investment created a vertical weaving and knitting facility in American Park Free Zone, El Salvador. That plant produces elastics and webbings from ¼ inch to 12 inches wide and includes in‑house dyeing and finishing, rotary printing, cutting and sewing, performance finishes, and custom packaging. Two dedicated research and development divisions support new product development and custom design for brands.

The company serves a broad range of end markets, including swim, dance, and yoga apparel; underwear waistbands and trims; ballistic protection for military uniforms and law‑enforcement body armor; work apparel and flame‑resistant uniforms; safety and industrial protective equipment; team‑sports gear such as goggles, pads, and helmets; performance compression and activewear; and orthopedic, medical, and stretch‑loop products requiring latex‑free, hook‑receptive surfaces.

George C. Moore emphasizes continual innovation and customer support as its founding premise, citing competitive pricing, consistent quality, and on‑time delivery as reasons it has remained a preferred supplier for over 110 years. Sustainability initiatives have cut heating and cooling energy use by 35%, lighting energy by 40%, and water‑usage ratio by 44%, while recycling programs reuse wooden pallets, cardboard, and plastic bags.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Narrow elastic weaving", "Narrow elastic knitting", "Wide warp knit fabric manufacturing", "Dyeing and finishing", "Rotary printing", "Cutting and sewing", "Performance finishes application", "Custom packaging", "Design and engineering support", "Research and development", "Technical consultation", "Jacquard elastic production", "Printed elastic production"], "industries": ["Swimwear", "Dancewear", "Yoga apparel", "Underwear", "Ballistic protection", "Military uniforms", "Law enforcement", "Work apparel", "Uniforms", "Safety equipment", "Industrial protective equipment", "Team sports equipment", "Performance compression", "Active apparel", "Orthopedic medical", "Stretch loop medical"], "materials": ["Sustainable yarns (natural)", "Sustainable yarns (recycled)", "Latex-free elastic", "Hook receptive fabrics", "Plush surface fabrics", "Flame resistant finishes", "Technical performance finishes"], "equipment": ["Vertical weaving lines", "Vertical knitting lines", "Rotary printing equipment", "Dyeing and finishing equipment", "Cutting and sewing equipment"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Two dedicated R&D divisions for narrow elastic innovation", "Vertical manufacturing in El Salvador with in-house dyeing, finishing, rotary printing, and sewing", "Over 110 years as a family-owned narrow fabric manufacturer", "Energy consumption reduced 35% in heating/cooling and 40% in lighting since recent upgrades", "Water usage ratio reduced 44% through process optimization"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1909 in Westerly, Rhode Island -> /about-us", "Family-owned, privately held parent of two divisions (George C. Moore Company and Darlington Fabrics) -> /about-us", "US headquarters in Westerly with sales, engineering, design, R&D, technical support -> /about-us", "El Salvador facility established 2006 in American Park Free Zone, vertical weaving/knitting, 1/4\" to 12\" width -> /about-us", "In-house dyeing & finishing, rotary printing, cutting & sewing, performance finishes, custom packaging -> /about-us", "Two R&D divisions for innovation and custom design -> /about-us", "Industries served: swim/dance/yoga, underwear, ballistic protection, work apparel, safety/industrial, team sports, performance compression, orthopedic/medical/stretch loop -> /", "Sustainability: 35% energy reduction heating/cooling, 40% lighting, 33% equipment, 22% fuel oil; 44% water usage reduction; recycling of pallets, cardboard, plastic bags -> /about-us", "Company describes itself as ''leading manufacturer of narrow elastic fabric and rigid webbing in the Western Hemisphere'' -> /", "Headquarters city/state from database -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "manufacturer of stretch and rigid narrow fabric (woven and knit)", "founded_year": "1909", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='george-c-moore' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='George''s Apparel has operated in Manchester, New Hampshire, for over three decades. The business occupies a corner location on Elm Street and Central Avenue, serving customers from across New England. No founding year, ownership structure, or founder names are disclosed in the company''s public materials.

The shop functions as a traditional haberdashery, retailing men''s formal wear including suits, jackets, dress shirts, and footwear. It carries brands such as Ralph Lauren, Calvin Klein, S. Cohen, Mantoni, Michael Kors, and Hart Schaffner & Marx, along with footwear from Florsheim, Clarks, Johnston & Murphy, and Bostonian. A fully staffed tailor shop provides alterations on garments purchased in-store as well as on items brought in from elsewhere. A dedicated wedding shop assists entire wedding parties with suit and tuxedo selection.

