UPDATE companies SET description='Gil Sewing Corp. operates from Morton Grove, Illinois, a Chicago suburb. The company traces its roots to 1992 when Michael Kaham started the business with a handful of seamstresses; it was formally established as a Women Minority Owned Business on May 20, 1993. Now a family-owned operation, it has grown to employ several hundred seamstresses in a 56,000-square-foot, fully automated facility.

The company provides turnkey apparel manufacturing: design, development, cutting, sewing, embroidery, and full-package production. Its domestic plant runs Gerber GtXL cutters capable of 30-ply lays and computerized servo-motor sewing machines. It handles small to large-scale runs for uniforms, tailored garments, outerwear, knits, fire-resistant apparel, and non-apparel items such as dog coats and upholstery. Overseas production is managed through partner factories in nine countries, with patterns and samples developed in Chicago before shipment.

Clients include major uniform suppliers, fashion brands, and the U.S. military—specifically the Naval Center for Research and Testing. The company holds DOD certification for final audit testing and maintains a sub-2.5 AQL across domestic and offshore orders. Its customer base spans retail, defense, activewear, and specialty markets.

Founder Michael Kaham’s emphasis on perfection and family values drives the company’s quality system, which includes in-process auditing at every operation and dedicated auditors who travel to overseas partners. The firm promotes its domestic-first development model and quick-turn shipping—anywhere in the U.S. within three days—as key differentiators.', certifications=ARRAY['DOD certified for final audit testing']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Design", "Development", "Cutting (Gerber GtXL)", "Sewing (computerized servo-motor)", "Embroidery (custom, contract)", "Full-package production", "Sourcing (domestic and overseas)", "Quality auditing (in-process, final, overseas)", "Pattern making", "Sample development", "Tech pack creation", "Overseas production management"], "industries": ["Uniforms", "Fashion apparel", "Retail apparel", "Military/Defense", "Pet apparel", "Upholstery", "Activewear", "Fire-resistant apparel"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Gerber GtXL cutters", "Computerized servo-motor sewing machines"], "volume": "Small to large scale production", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["56,000 sq ft fully automated Chicago-area facility", "Gerber GtXL cutters (up to 30 ply) and servo-motor sewing machines", "DOD-certified quality with <2.5 AQL", "Domestic pattern development and sample approval before overseas production", "In-house custom embroidery and sourcing from 9 countries"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1992 by Michael Kaham -> /", "Formally established as Women Minority Owned Business on May 20, 1993 -> /about-us", "Family-owned company -> /", "Headquarters in Morton Grove, Illinois -> db", "56,000 sq ft fully automated facility in Chicago -> /about-us", "Gerber GtXL cutters up to 30 ply -> /about-us", "Computerized servo-motor sewing machines -> /about-us", "In-house custom and contract embroidery -> /services", "Sourcing from 9 countries -> /services", "DOD certified for final audit testing -> /about-us", "Less than 2.5 AQL quality standard -> /about-us", "Domestic development before overseas production -> /about-us", "Partner factories in Mexico, China, El Salvador, Thailand, Vietnam, Kenya, Ethiopia, Egypt -> /about-us", "Serves uniform, fashion, military, retail, pet, upholstery, activewear, FR apparel markets -> /, /about-us", "Quick turn times, ship anywhere in US within three days -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We are a garment manufacture of male and female uniforms, tailored and work clothing and retail apparel.", "founded_year": "1993", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Minority-owned", "Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='gil-sewing-corp' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Glaser Steel has operated in Colorado Springs, Colorado, since 1945 when Eugene Glaser and his brother-in-law Frank Holley opened H & G Welding in a former horse stable downtown. The business became Glaser Welding Works under Eugene’s sole ownership, with his wife Darlene handling bookkeeping, and later transitioned to the Glaser Steel name. It remains a family-owned enterprise, now led by the third generation—Jacque Glaser Jensen and her husband Tony Jensen—after successive stewardship by their son Burton “Buddy” Glaser and his wife Charolette.

The company stocks mild steel and aluminum in full lengths or cut-to-size, and maintains a drop pile for remnant pieces. Its shop at 619 South 31st Street, occupied since 1969, provides custom saw cutting, shearing, drilling, punching, welding and fabrication, and CNC plasma cutting of sheet and plate; a 2005 expansion added a plasma table and dedicated sheet storage. The firm also delivers materials and finished fabrications to local job sites.

Glaser Steel serves customers across the Colorado Front Range, supplying raw steel and fabricated components for projects ranging from ornamental railings and window covers to structural fabrications. The business does not list specific industry sectors but works with anyone requiring steel supply or custom metalwork.

