UPDATE companies SET description='Global Plastics was founded in 1992 in Indianapolis, Indiana, starting with a single 40-ton Nissei injection molding machine. The company has grown from those humble beginnings into a vertically integrated molder with a fleet of more than 70 injection molding machines, an in-house full-service tooling department, product development engineers, and project management staff. A 250,000-square-foot warehousing and distribution facility serves Global Plastics and three affiliate companies—Global Forming, Global Packaging, and Global Air—allowing production from design through delivery under one roof.

The molder serves customers in medical device, automotive, and food packaging sectors, holding ISO 13485, IATF 16949, and SQF certifications alongside ISO 9001. Its capabilities span rapid prototyping, design-for-manufacturability review, secondary operations, and high-volume production tooling.

Global Plastics emphasizes a vertically integrated model that keeps engineering, tooling, and molding under one roof, which the company says shortens lead times and improves responsiveness. A dedicated customer-service representative is assigned to each account, and a cross-functional continuous-improvement team meets weekly to refine processes and adopt new automation such as robots and collaborative robots.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001','ISO 13485','IATF 16949','SQF']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Plastic injection molding", "In-house tooling design and fabrication", "Product development and design support", "Design for manufacturability (DFM)", "Project management", "Rapid prototyping", "Secondary operations", "Warehousing and distribution"], "industries": ["Medical devices", "Automotive", "Food packaging"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["70+ injection molding machines", "Nissei 40-ton injection molding machine", "Robots and collaborative robots"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Vertically integrated engineering, tooling, and molding under one roof", "Dedicated customer-service representative per account", "Weekly cross-functional continuous-improvement team", "250,000 sq ft warehousing and distribution facility", "In-house full-service tooling department"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1992 with 40-ton Nissei machine -> /about-us", "70+ injection molding machines -> /about-us", "In-house full-service tooling department -> /about-us", "Product development and project management expertise -> /about-us", "250,000 sq ft warehousing and distribution facility -> /about-us", "Three affiliate companies: Global Forming, Global Packaging, Global Air -> /about-us", "Vertically integrated engineering, tooling, production under one roof -> /", "Dedicated customer service representative per account -> /about-us", "Cross-functional continuous improvement team meets weekly -> /about-us", "Robots and co-bots used -> /about-us", "Certifications: ISO 9001, ISO 13485, IATF 16949, SQF -> /", "Serves medical device, automotive, food packaging industries (implied by certifications) -> /", "Rapid prototyping -> /", "Design for manufacturability support -> /", "Secondary operations -> /", "Strategic location Indianapolis, Indiana -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Global Plastics is a full-service plastic injection molding service provider", "founded_year": "1992", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='global-plastics' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Globe Equipment Company operates from Bridgeport, Connecticut, where it was founded in 1938 by the grandfather of current leadership and his brother. The business remains family-owned, now in its third generation under Brian Ringelheim, who joined formally in 2004, working alongside his father, Jay. The company describes its team as "industry born and bred," with several employees staying for decades.

The company supplies a broad range of commercial kitchen equipment, food service supplies, and operational essentials. Its product categories include bar equipment, concession equipment, dinnerware, glassware, flatware, janitorial supplies, and kitchen tools. Beyond distribution, Globe provides drafting and planning services, product selection consultation, fabrication coordination, and installation management. It offers scheduled local delivery in its region and coordinated national shipping for larger orders.

Globe serves restaurants, bars, concession operations, and senior living communities. Its customer base includes independent restaurants such as La Cucina, multi-site senior living operators like Covenant Living, and entrepreneurs expanding grab‑and‑go concepts.

Globe emphasizes a consultative approach, aiming to understand each customer’s operational challenges and budget constraints. The leadership frames its differentiation around long‑term relationships, value‑engineering suggestions, and a willingness to "give our people a little extra leeway to deliver on their promises." The goal is to retain customers for decades, supporting the company’s own ambition to remain in business for another 80-plus years.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Commercial kitchen equipment distribution", "Food service supplies distribution", "Bar equipment and supplies", "Concession equipment", "Dinnerware, glassware, flatware supply", "Janitorial supplies", "Kitchen tools supply", "Kitchen and workspace design", "Product selection consultation", "Installation management", "Fabrication coordination", "Local delivery", "National shipping"], "industries": ["Restaurant", "Senior living", "Foodservice", "Hospitality", "Concession"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Family-owned, third-generation business since 1938", "Consultative foodservice equipment selection and value engineering", "Drafting, planning, and installation management services", "Scheduled local delivery and coordinated national shipping", "Deep experience with restaurant and senior living sectors"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1938 -> db", "Headquarters Bridgeport, CT -> db", "Family-owned, third generation -> /about-us", "Brian Ringelheim and father Jay -> /about-us", "Product categories: bar, concession, dinnerware, glassware, flatware, janitorial, kitchen -> /", "Services: drafting, planning, product selection, installation management -> /", "Delivery: local scheduled, national shipping -> /", "Industries: restaurant, senior living, concession -> /, /about-us", "Customer examples: Covenant Living, La Cucina, grab-n-go concept -> /", "Consultative approach, value engineering -> /", "LinkedIn U